## 🎯 The Art of Executable Combat

### ⚡ Activation Spells: Running Executable Files

Items that end with `*` are **executable encounters** - programs, scripts, and
magical artifacts that you can activate and wield:

```bash
./treasure      # Activate the treasure chest in this room
./potion        # Consume a magical potion for enhancement
```

### 🔍 Understanding the Dot Path Magic

The `./` prefix is a **relative path incantation**:

- **`.`** = "Here in this exact chamber" (current directory)
- **`/`** = Path separator between location and item name
- **`./item`** = "Execute the item located here in this room"

### 🧭 Navigation Between Battle Zones

Master these movement spells for tactical positioning:

```bash
cd ..           # Retreat one level up (parent directory)
cd chamber      # Advance into the inner chamber
cd ~            # Teleport to your home base
cd /            # Travel to the root of all domains
```

## 🛡️ Advanced Combat Techniques

### 🎲 Relative vs Absolute Path Combat

**Relative Paths** (position-based):

```bash
./treasure           # Item in current chamber
../treasure          # Item in the chamber above
chamber/spell        # Item in the chamber sub-room
```

**Absolute Paths** (location-specific):

```bash
/usr/bin/ls          # System command at exact location
~/documents/script   # File in your home territory
```

### 🔐 Permission Mastery: The `chmod` Enchantment

Some items may need permission adjustments before you can wield them:

```bash
ls -l item          # Inspect item permissions and properties
chmod +x item       # Grant execution permissions (make executable)
chmod 755 item      # Set full combat readiness (read, write, execute)
```

